WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.631 --> 00:00:08.383
Um, I can't see a thing!

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:14.431
A face? A giant robot!

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:18.351
You won't find this
in the orientation book.

00:00:19.227 --> 00:00:22.981
This is the ultimate multipurpose decisive
combat weapons system created by man.

00:00:23.314 --> 00:00:25.275
The Artificial Human Evangelion.

00:00:25.567 --> 00:00:26.735
Unit 01 of the series.

00:00:27.402 --> 00:00:29.487
Built in complete secrecy,

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:32.240
this is mankind's very last trump card.

00:00:32.407 --> 00:00:35.285
-This is part of my father's work?
-Correct.

00:00:37.245 --> 00:00:38.246
It's been a while.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.124
Father...

00:00:43.793 --> 00:00:44.794
Launch the Eva.

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:48.840
Launch the Eva?
But Unit 00 is still grounded!

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.677
Wait, you want to use Unit 01?!

00:00:53.511 --> 00:00:54.846
There's no other choice.

00:00:55.096 --> 00:00:58.141
Wait just a second!
Rei's in no condition for that!

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:00.185
It's got no pilot!

00:01:01.186 --> 00:01:02.353
He just arrived.

00:01:03.688 --> 00:01:04.689
Are you serious?

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:07.192
-Shinji Ikari.
-Yes?

00:01:07.776 --> 00:01:08.860
You're going to pilot it.

00:01:09.819 --> 00:01:14.866
But it took even Rei Ayanami seven months
to synchronize with her Eva!

00:01:14.991 --> 00:01:17.577
He literally just got here!
He couldn't possibly do it!

00:01:17.702 --> 00:01:20.455
All I ask is that he sit in the cockpit.
Nothing more.

00:01:20.538 --> 00:01:21.539
But...

00:01:21.623 --> 00:01:23.958
Repelling that Angel
is our number one priority right now.

00:01:24.793 --> 00:01:29.506
For that, we need anyone capable of
synchronizing with an Eva to try,

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:30.882
however remote the chances.

00:01:32.008 --> 00:01:34.260
I shouldn't need to tell you this,
Capt. Katsuragi.

00:01:36.471 --> 00:01:37.597
You're right.

00:01:39.349 --> 00:01:41.392
Father... Why did you send for me?

00:01:41.726 --> 00:01:43.812
For the reason you're thinking.

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:47.982
So you want me to get inside this
and fight that thing out there?

00:01:48.316 --> 00:01:49.150
Correct.

00:01:49.484 --> 00:01:52.445
I don't want to do that!
Why send for me after all this time?!

00:01:53.196 --> 00:01:55.406
I thought you left me
because you didn't need me!

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:57.826
I do now, so I sent for you.

00:02:00.537 --> 00:02:02.038
But why me?

00:02:02.539 --> 00:02:04.791
Because it's impossible for anyone else.

00:02:05.583 --> 00:02:09.671
It is for me, too. I've never seen
or heard of this thing before.

00:02:09.921 --> 00:02:11.297
I can't possibly do it!

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:13.383
Learn how.

00:02:14.259 --> 00:02:18.012
That's... That's impossible!

00:02:18.888 --> 00:02:20.765
There's no way I can pilot this!

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:25.353
If you're going to pilot it, do it.
Otherwise, get out!

00:02:37.115 --> 00:02:39.284
That bastard must have figured out
where we are.

00:02:43.204 --> 00:02:45.206
Shinji, we don't have much time.

00:02:50.211 --> 00:02:51.462
Get in.

00:02:52.463 --> 00:02:56.968
No way. I just got here! This is crazy!

00:02:58.386 --> 00:03:01.723
Tell me, Shinji. Why did you come?

00:03:03.725 --> 00:03:07.896
Don't run away! Not from your father,
and especially not from yourself.

00:03:08.438 --> 00:03:12.525
I know! But there's no way I can do this!

